{"id":"37b5dd94-3162-4bce-8f7a-50e61ffe80e0","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"c333c34c359e6c2b","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/worker/process.ts","baseline":{"blob":"9c49ce2df377f90aa6e7201da39d46348a28db37","start":244,"end":286},"shape":{"type":"ExportDeclaration","atoms":["export","const","listening","=","new","Set","<","number",">","(",")"]},"context":{"before":"37f0cb7f9ea453b1","after":"aa74e5b459e506d1"}},"payload":{"text":"The ports a debug run's servers listen on (node:http, from almostnode): each answers the preview (`virtual.debug.<port>`,\nasked by the dev-server worker) and keeps the run alive — out of work, it idles, serving.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:23:53.780Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:23:53.780Z"}
{"id":"44ac7482-cd7d-467e-80b7-61da77792904","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"1f9cc8e4c640de76","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/worker/process.ts","baseline":{"blob":"b1f0d79680069beba86d7a60b95f5f1f2ebf425e","start":3330,"end":3368},"shape":{"type":"ExportDeclaration","atoms":["export","const","held","=","new","Set","<","unknown",">","(",")"]},"context":{"before":"6bec6af8c2428dd7","after":"c20ec7f57bb6b717"}},"payload":{"text":"What holds a debug run open — almostnode's keep-alive hook (`__nodeKeepAlive`): a server is held from the moment\nit's told to listen (its port is known a microtask later), let go when it closes or is unref'd.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:23:23.182Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:23:23.182Z"}
{"id":"96e38e92-fd0d-477b-b0e4-4681dad58c6d","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"8f29fb6038ad867b","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/worker/process.ts","baseline":{"blob":"c5c816f7821d986b86d14aed5a4b416a2346b888","start":2956,"end":3000},"shape":{"type":"ExportDeclaration","atoms":["export","const","EXITED","=","Symbol","(","\"","process.exit","\"",")"]},"context":{"before":"aa74e5b459e506d1","after":"6bec6af8c2428dd7"}},"payload":{"text":"`process.exit(code)` out of the program (capabilitySurface): the run ends there with `code`, as node's does — not a\ncrash. Caught where a run's end is decided.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:23:27.519Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:23:27.519Z"}
{"id":"a934982e-68b0-4069-8687-a9633b6050b3","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"8f29fb6038ad867b","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/worker/process.ts","baseline":{"blob":"403f6137f033ac05f164d610b79a9906c622a597","start":2364,"end":2408},"shape":{"type":"ExportDeclaration","atoms":["export","const","EXITED","=","Symbol","(","\"","process.exit","\"",")"]},"context":{"before":"aa74e5b459e506d1","after":"6bec6af8c2428dd7"}},"payload":{"text":"A debugged tsval run gets the SAME zero-authority capability surface the canary uses (shared `capabilityStandins`):\n`fetch` and node builtins (`node:fs`, `node:child_process`, …) resolve to inert, effect-free stand-ins, and any\nOTHER import resolves to a recursive inert proxy. Without this the guest crashes on the first `import` of a node\nbuiltin (there is no real module system in the worker) BEFORE reaching a capability breakpoint — the whole point of\nthe hard-stop. Real effects belong to the almostnode \"production\" adapter, not to tsval's reverse-steppable VM.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:23:35.132Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:23:35.132Z"}
{"id":"bf519746-b20c-4142-b910-3df474daab45","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"6a26c28d250a2c91","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/worker/process.ts","baseline":{"blob":"35ffb6cd7ebabcca909865b0f7e637e00f9a6599","start":3760,"end":3971},"shape":{"type":"ExportDeclaration","atoms":["export","function","typed","(","message",":","Extract","<","Control",",","{","\"","type","\"",":","\"","stdin","\"","}",">",")",":","void","{","if","(","message",".","end","===","true",")","{","stdin",".","emit","(","\"","end","\"",")",";","}","else","{","stdin",".","emit","(","\"","data","\"",",","message",".","data",")",";","}","state",".","current","?.","loop","?.","wake","?.","(",")",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"c20ec7f57bb6b717"}},"payload":{"text":"Typed in the Debug Console or the terminal it was started in: the program's input — its listeners called with it\n(or, at its end, told so), and the run woken to go on.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:23:09.847Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:23:09.847Z"}
{"id":"d016343f-bcb5-4775-ac2d-fc4010f86d07","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"51fba4146486575d","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/worker/process.ts","baseline":{"blob":"957275e90a80ce02e93994734b02e841230b1011","start":0,"end":48},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","type","{","Control","}","from","\"","../debug-protocol","\""]},"context":{"after":"37f0cb7f9ea453b1"}},"payload":{"text":"The program's process, as a terminal's run has it: its stdin (what's typed there), the servers it listens with, what\nholds it open, and its exit.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:24:11.456Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:24:11.456Z"}
